From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domsvoboda <domsvoboda@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:36:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: Give a process the package identity of the
 AppxManifest.xml above its image.

GetCurrentPackageFullName, GetCurrentPackageFamilyName,
GetCurrentPackagePath, GetCurrentApplicationUserModelId,
GetCurrentPackageId and GetCurrentPackageInfo (the head package only)
answered APPMODEL_ERROR_NO_PACKAGE for every process. An unpacked
Store/GDK install keeps its AppxManifest.xml at the package root: look
for it in up to 16 directories above the main image, resolved through
its Unix name so a symlinked helper does not take the package of the
link's directory, parse its Identity and Applications, and derive the
publisher id (SHA-256 of the publisher, Crockford base32) and the
family, full name and AUMID from them. A process with no such manifest
still has no package.

Ported from Xodus Nexus (its wine-appmodel-identity.patch) onto
WineHQ, which replaced libtomcrypt with SymCrypt: the publisher id's
SHA-256 is SymCrypt's, with the SymCrypt environment ntdll also
defines.

Ported-from: https://github.com/domsvoboda/nexus-wine/commit/873e6a633d29dc62b8ffb59b5fa598545d28986a
Ported: adapted
Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-30-xbox-ground-truth-nexus.md
Offered-upstream: no
